<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Commandments of Valhalla</h1>
<p>In the beginning the Creators of Valhalla laid down the following 
commandments for all players to follow. These commandments were 
designed by the creators to keep Valhalla fun and enjoyable for 
everyone, players as well as Administrators of the world. Failure to 
comply with the following commandments will be dealt with by punishment, 
based on severity of offense as well as the type of infraction.
</p><p><b>I.</b> Sexual harrassment of other characters on here will NOT be 
tolerated, and will result in immediate dismissal from the game.
</p><p><b>II.</b> More than two characters controlled by the same player on line 
at the same time are not allowed on Valhalla. People logging on more 
than 2 characters at a time will result in all of the players 
characters dismissal from Valhalla.
</p><p><b>III.</b> Exploiting a bug will result in immediate punishment of the 
player involved. If you think you have found a bug, please contact the 
Administrators of Valhalla. They will handle it or give you further 
instructions on what to do. If you are not sure about a bug or not, then 
please inform the Administrator(s) and do not exploit the bug.
</p><p><b>IV.</b> Player killing is only allowed between two people who have 
signed the book of blood. Anything to do with player killing is also 
only allowed between two people who have signed the book of blood. Any 
action taken by someone who is not in the book of blood to help or 
hinder during a pk fight is also in violation of the pk rules. Only 
thieves that have signed the book can steal from other players but only 
from players who have also signed the book. Violating the Pk rules can 
have varying punishments from a warning to the entire banning of all 
your characters so when in doubt don't get involved in a pk fight.
</p><p><b>V.</b> Obscene or offensive language will not be tolerated in any of 
the public channels. We also insist that all usage of public channels be 
in english, there is no way we can determine that what you expressed in 
another language was or was not offensive, so all such use on public 
comms will be considered offensive. Public channels being shout and 
newbie. What you do in the privacy of a room is up to you and others in 
the room. Abusing the public channels in anyway can and will result in 
your character losing his abilities to use those public channels. Do not 
mail the administrator who No-shouts you begging to be un-no-shouted, 
doing so may cause your no-shout time to be extended or made permament.
</p><p><b>VI.</b> Please be polite and courteous to other players. Remember that 
they are here to enjoy this mud and we want them to all have equal 
opportunity to enjoy Valhalla. Overly annoying and excessively obnoxious 
characters will be dealt with. We want everyone to enjoy their time 
here, world Administrators as well as players.
</p><p><b>VII.</b> If you think an action is questionable, then simply refrain 
from doing it. The Administration reserves the right to make judgements 
on whether an action is wrong or not. We are only human and cannot 
possible think of all the various illegal and legal actions on the mud.
</p><p><b>VIII.</b> Players are responsible to read ALL boards and 
announcements. If a warning is posted and you do not read it, yet break 
that rule, you will be held responsible for the offense. So please take 
the 2-3 minutes time when you log on to read the boards.
</p><p><b>IX.</b> Asking an Administrator to give you an object, heal you, or 
help you advance in the mud in anyway is a violation. Please save your 
breath and our time and don't ask things of Administrators, which you 
KNOW they won't do.
</p><p><b>X.</b> The use of Robots or computer controlled characters are illegal 
on Valhalla. This means if you are not controlling the actions of your 
character it is illegal. Players found using robots will have all 
characters dismissed from Valhalla.
</p><p><b>XI.</b> Keep in mind that we punish the PLAYER and not the character. 
Thus if you are found guilty of some offense all of your characters can 
be punished. Punishment of all characters is not all ways the case but 
in extreme circumstances is the only option. It is best to be mature 
and take account for your actions. The Administration is not here to 
hurt you, but to make sure everyone is treated fairly and with respect.
</p><p><br />
